  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#1460\", \"PowerToys#6616\", \"PowerToys#3676\"], \"answer\": \"Both requests have been reported before. Per-keyboard remapping (laptop vs. external USB keyboard) is tracked in the main ticket PowerToys#1460, and PowerToys#6616 and PowerToys#3676 were closed as duplicates of it. It isn't currently possible. Windows public APIs don't let PowerToys tell which keyboard a keypress came from, so that would need driver-level support. For now, Keyboard Manager remaps apply to all keyboards. The brightness request is tracked separately in PowerToys#4450 (remap a key to brightness up/down). PowerToys has no brightness command yet, so Keyboard Manager can't map to one today. Follow those tickets for updates.\"}",
